            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^ { \\circ } a ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . What do you observe? You will find that the mean determined in each case is the same, i.e., 62. (Why ?)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.343,
            0.901,
            0.381
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, we can say that the value of the mean obtained does not depend on the choice of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^ { \\circ } a ^ { \\prime }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.386,
            0.902,
            0.447
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Observe that in Table 13.4, the values in Column 4 are all multiples of 15. So, if we divide the values in the entire Column 4 by 15, we would get smaller numbers to multiply with "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "f _ { i ^ { * } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (Here, 15 is the class size of each class interval.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.461,
            0.844,
            0.5
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "u _ { _ i } = \\frac { x _ { _ i } - a } { h }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , where a is the assumed mean and h is the class size."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.508,
            0.901,
            0.549
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, we calculate "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "u _ { _ i }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in this way and continue as before (i.e., find "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "f _ { i }   u _ { i }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and then "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Sigma f _ { i } u _ { i } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Taking "
            },
